# T_SCRR: the user list and a new user.  The name is upper-cased as
# typed; Ctrl-S without a level puts the cursor on it; a password too short
# is refused by the server (its text shown on the password); one whose
# repetition differs is refused before any request; then the user is
# added (the request is checked by T_SCRR) and the list shows it.  A
# second new user named as an existing one is answered "Already exists"
# on the name, and Esc leaves after asking to discard.
S USERS
K INS
T bob
K TAB
T Bob Smith
K TAB
T ops
K TAB TAB
T abc
K TAB
T abc
K CTRL-S
S NOLEVEL
K SPACE SPACE CTRL-S
S SHORTPW
K CTRL-Y
T abc1
K TAB CTRL-Y
T abc2
K CTRL-S
S NOMATCH
K CTRL-Y
T abc1
K CTRL-S
S ADDED
K INS
T oper
K TAB TAB TAB SPACE TAB
T pass1
K TAB
T pass1
K CTRL-S
S DUPUSER
K ESC
S DISCARDQ
T Y
S BACK
K ESC
